            <ArticleTitle>[Study of the functioning of a membrane oxygenator MOST-122 during artificial circulation with pulsed blood flow].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>21-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Functioning of membrane oxygenator &quot;MOCT-122&quot; in pulsed operation of bypass in treadmil tests and during clinical perfusions was investigated. It was established that the inclusion of the oxygenator into the test line lead to a considerable decrease in parasitic pulsations both of rate and pressure. The pulsatory character of the flow was observed though the transconductance of increase and decrease fronts of the rate (as the result of oxygenator &quot;MOCT-122&quot; installation) demonstrated their satisfactory functioning.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
